<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sobekneferu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1777–1773 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century-bce">18th century BCE</a> · Also known as Sobekneferure</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sobekneferu was the last ruler of the Twelfth Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, reigning for nearly four years in the late nineteenth century BCE. Probably a daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amenemhat-iii">Amenemhat III</a>, she succeeded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amenemhat-iv">Amenemhat IV</a> and is the first woman known for certain to have taken the full royal titles of a king. Her death ended the dynasty and opened the Thirteenth Dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sobekneferu.jpg" alt="Sobekneferu" width="320" height="444" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hedwig Fechheimer (1871-1942), Die Plastik der Ägypter, Berlin 1914, pl. 57 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statue_of_Sobekneferu_(Berlin_Egyptian_Museum_14475).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
